    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a challenging slate today, but the optimizer has identified two primary engines for offensive production. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.13) is our undisputed strongest play; his leadoff spot against a favorable matchup (4.06 xERA) combined with a massive 14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage creates an elite scoring environment. He is followed closely by **Yordan Alvarez** (62.19), whose elite 0.465 xwOBA remains the backbone of our lineup, and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.18), who leverages a premium leadoff slot to mitigate the challenge of facing a decent arm in Kremer. **Junior Caminero** (60.55) also secures a top-tier spot, benefiting from a high-leverage 3-hole assignment that outweighs his minor park-factor penalty.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully with **Christian Yelich** (39.81), whose score dips below our 40.0 floor due to a brutal matchup against the elite Skubal (2.77 xERA) and an unfavorable platoon split. **Gary Sanchez** (42.83) narrowly survives the cut, though his value is heavily suppressed by the same Skubal matchup. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Nelson Velazquez** (40.76). While he technically cleared the floor, the combination of a high-difficulty opponent in Bryan Woo and the uncertainty of a pending lineup position forced him to the bench in favor of the higher-upside profiles of **Carson Benge** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Gary Sanchez**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Yordan Alvarez**; as of this report, their spots are assumed. While **Caleb Durbin** faces a solid arm, his value is bolstered by his elite sprint speed and a matchup against a slow-delivery pitcher that creates a high-probability opportunity for stolen bases\u2014our most precious category. We will monitor weather reports and confirmed batting orders for **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich** closely, as any move down in the order could push them below the rosterable threshold for the day.",
